    description: "Residual found by the 2026-11-02 drain's A/B of the companion-object owner fix (the WI-vidof regression). With method owners resolved by position, 9 sbt call sites (and 2 on gatling) lose a resolution that dev had only BY ACCIDENT: a bare call to a member of a companion OBJECT, brought in by an import, e.g. sbt main-settings Structure.scala:834 `extendScoped(..)` inside `object SettingKey`, with `import Scoped.extendScoped` at line 717 and the definition in `object Scoped` (line 673); Parser.scala `mkFailure(..)` calls into object Parser. On dev those methods were credited to the same-named TRAIT and the inherited-calls linker reached them through that misassignment. The correct route is the analyzer binding a bare name through an explicit `import Obj.member` / `import Obj.*` -- the WI-tipoh / WI-kipol import-reading path, not the linker. Record: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_queue_11022026/fix_ab/."  # bb69
